# Adaptive & Responsive Design Upgrade

I have implemented a comprehensive update to ensure the GHG Reporting dashboard and calculation tools adapt perfectly to any screen size, from wide desktops to mobile phones.

## Key Improvements

### 1. Fluid Desktop Scaling
Resolved the issue where the dashboard appeared "larger than the browser" on smaller laptops.
- **Global Box-Sizing**: Applied `border-box` reset to ensure padding doesn't push elements beyond their intended width.
- **Auto-Fit Grids**: The dashboard grid now uses fluid `minmax` values, allowing it to scale naturally on 13" laptops and ultra-wide monitors.
- **Overflow Fixes**: Standardized scroll behavior to prevent "double scrollbars" and ensure the main container stays within the viewport.

### 2. Mobile Responsive Sidebar
Implemented a modern "Drawer" navigation for touch devices.
- **Hamburger Menu**: Added a sleek SVG toggle button to the top bar on mobile and tablet views.
- **Drawer Animation**: The sidebar now slides in from the left with a smooth transition.
- **Soft Overlay**: Added a blur-effect overlay when the menu is open, allowing users to tap anywhere outside to close the menu.

### 3. Stacking Grid Layouts
The multi-column dashboard now intelligently stacks into a single column on mobile devices.
- **Card Priority**: Critical metrics and charts stay on top, while secondary lists (like the Recent Activity) stack below.
- **Touch-Friendly Inputs**: Adjusted padding and font sizes for better readability and tap targets on mobile.
- **Table Interactivity**: Heavy data tables now feature horizontal scroll containers to prevent layout breaking.

## Technical Details
- **CSS Breakpoints**: Tablet (`1024px`) and Mobile (`768px`).
- **Logic**: Centralized in [mobile-menu.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/mobile-menu.js).
- **Styles**: Integrated into the core [dashboard-dark.css](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard-dark.css).

## How to Test
1. **Desktop**: Notice how the cards now fit more comfortably on your screen without horizontal scroll.
2. **Resize**: Shrink your browser window to see the sidebar transform into a hamburger menu.
3. **Mobile View**: Open the site on a phone to experience the vertical scroll and drawer navigation.
